{"id":"neet-2026-q156","pn":156,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Bt toxin genes","q":"The toxin proteins isolated from Bacillus thuringiensis, coded by which of the following genes would control cotton bollworms and corn borer, respectively?","o":["cryIAc and cryIIIAb","cryIAc and cryIIAb","cryIAc and cryIAb","cryIIAb and cryIAc"],"c":2,"s":"Bt toxin genes were isolated from Bacillus thuringiensis and put into crop plants such as cotton.\nThe choice of gene depends on the crop and the target pest, as most Bt toxins are specific to an insect group.\nThe toxin is coded by a gene named cry.\nThe proteins coded by cryIAc and cryIIAb control cotton bollworms, and the one coded by cryIAb controls corn borer.\nSo cryIAc for cotton bollworms and cryIAb for corn borer, which is option 3."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q162","pn":162,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Transgenic animals: products","q":"The human protein named α-1-antitrypsin, obtained from transgenic animals, is used for the treatment of ____ .","o":["Alzheimer's disease","Emphysema","Rheumatoid arthritis","Cystic fibrosis"],"c":1,"s":"The correct answer is option 2.\nThe human protein α-1-antitrypsin, obtained from transgenic animals, is used to treat emphysema.\nTransgenic models also exist for the study of other diseases such as Alzheimer's disease, rheumatoid arthritis and cystic fibrosis."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q144","pn":144,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"RNA interference","q":"Silencing of specific mRNA is possible via RNAi because of","o":["Complementary dsRNA","Inhibitory ssRNA","Complementary tRNA","Non-complementary ssRNA"],"c":0,"s":"RNAi (RNA interference) takes place in all eukaryotic organisms as a method of cellular defence.\nIt silences a specific mRNA because of a complementary dsRNA molecule.\nThis dsRNA binds to the mRNA and prevents its translation."},
{"id":"neet-2024-q168","pn":168,"y":"NEET 2024 · 5 May","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Applications in medicine and agriculture","q":"Match List I with List II:\nA. α-1 antitrypsin — I. Cotton bollworm\nB. Cry IAb — II. ADA deficiency\nC. Cry IAc — III. Emphysema\nD. Enzyme replacement therapy — IV. Corn borer","o":["A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II","A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III","A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV"],"c":0,"s":"Option (1) is correct.\nα-1 antitrypsin is used to treat emphysema.\nCry IAb gene controls corn borer.\nCry IAc gene controls cotton bollworm.\nEnzyme replacement therapy can be used for ADA deficiency.\nNote: Option (4) is garbled in the paper; it is read as A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV."},
{"id":"neet-2024-q183","pn":183,"y":"NEET 2024 · 5 May","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Ti plasmid vector","q":"The “Ti plasmid” of Agrobacterium tumefaciens stands for","o":["Tumor inducing plasmid","Temperature independent plasmid","Tumour, inhibiting plasmid","Tumor independent plasmid"],"c":0,"s":"Ti plasmid of Agrobacterium tumefaciens means tumor inducing plasmid.\nIt carries T-DNA, which causes tumors in many dicot plants.\nOptions (2), (3) and (4) are wrong."},
{"id":"neet-2023-q151","pn":151,"y":"NEET 2023 · 7 May","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Molecular diagnosis","q":"Which one of the following techniques does not serve the purpose of early diagnosis of a disease for its early treatment?","o":["Enzyme Linked Immuno-Sorbent Assay (ELISA) technique","Recombinant DNA Technology","Serum and Urine analysis","Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) technique"],"c":2,"s":"Serum and urine analysis are conventional tests.\nThey cannot detect a disease early.\nRecombinant DNA technology, PCR and ELISA can detect a disease early, so they are used for early diagnosis."},
{"id":"neet-2022r-q181","pn":181,"y":"Re-NEET 2022 · 4 Sep","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Transgenic animals","q":"Milk of transgenic 'Cow Rosie' was nutritionally more balanced product for human babies than natural cow milk because it contained :","o":["Human enzyme Adenosine Deaminase (ADA)","Human protein -1-antitrypsin","Human alpha-lactalbumin","Human insulin-like growth factor"],"c":2,"s":"Rosie's milk contained the human protein alpha-lactalbumin.\nThis made it better balanced for human babies."},
{"id":"neet-2022-q190","pn":190,"y":"NEET 2022 · 17 Jul","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Genetically engineered insulin","q":"Statements related to human Insulin are given below. Which statement(s) is/are correct about genetically engineered Insulin? (a) Pro-hormone insulin contain extra stretch of C-peptide (b) A-peptide and B-peptide chains of insulin were produced separately in E.coli, extracted and combined by creating disulphide bond between them. (c) Insulin used for treating Diabetes was extracted from Cattles and Pigs. (d) Pro-hormone Insulin needs to be processed for converting into a mature and functional hormone. (e) Some patients develop allergic reactions to the foreign insulin. Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:","o":["(b) only","(c) and (d) only","(c), (d) and (e) only","(a), (b) and (d) only"],"c":0,"s":"In genetic engineering, the A and B chains are made separately in E. coli, extracted and joined by disulphide bonds, so (b) is correct.\n(a) is wrong: engineered insulin has no C-peptide.\n(c) is wrong: cattle and pig insulin is not genetically engineered.\n(d) is wrong: no processing of pro-insulin is needed since the chains are made separately.\n(e) is wrong: allergy is mostly seen with animal-derived insulin."},
{"id":"neet-2021-q168","pn":168,"y":"NEET 2021 · 12 Sep","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Molecular diagnosis","q":"For effective treatment of the disease, early diagnosis and understanding its pathophysiology is very important. Which of the following molecular diagnostic techniques is very useful for early detection?","o":["Hybridization Technique","Western Blotting Technique","Southern Blotting Technique","ELISA Technique"],"a":"3/4*","s":"ELISA detects antigens or antibodies of a pathogen, and can catch an infection early.\nSouthern blotting detects a specific DNA sequence, so pathogen DNA can be found even before antibodies form.\nHybridisation with probes is used to find mutated genes, and Western blotting detects a specific protein.\nSo both option 3 and option 4 can be argued as correct.\nNote: Printed key is \"3/4*\" (two options); not a plain 1-4."},
{"id":"neet-2021-q169","pn":169,"y":"NEET 2021 · 12 Sep","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Insulin","q":"With regard to insulin choose correct options.\n(a) C-peptide is not present in mature insulin.\n(b) The insulin produced by rDNA technology has Cpeptide.\n(c) The pro-insulin has C-peptide\n(d) A-peptide and B-peptide of insulin are interconnected by disulphide bridges.","o":["(a) and (d) only","(b) and (d) only","(b) and (c) only","(a), (c) and (d) only"],"c":3,"s":"Insulin is made as pro-insulin with chains A and B plus a C-peptide: (c) is true.\nThe C-peptide is cut out, so mature insulin has none: (a) true.\nRecombinant insulin is the mature form, so it has no C-peptide: (b) false.\nChains A and B are joined by disulphide bridges: (d) true.\nSo (a), (c) and (d)."},
{"id":"neet-2021-q179","pn":179,"y":"NEET 2021 · 12 Sep","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Biofortification","q":"Which of the following is not an objective of Biofortification in crops?","o":["Improve micronutrient and mineral content","Improve protein content","Improve resistance to diseases","Improve vitamin content"],"c":2,"s":"Biofortification breeds crops for better nutrition: more protein, vitamins, minerals and micronutrients.\nDisease resistance is a different breeding goal, so it is not an objective of biofortification."},
{"id":"neet-2021-q193","pn":193,"y":"NEET 2021 · 12 Sep","tp":"Biotechnology and its Applications","st":"Gene therapy for ADA deficiency","q":"The Adenosine deaminase deficiency results into","o":["Addison's disease","Dysfunction of Immune system","Parkinson's disease","Digestive disorder"],"c":1,"s":"Adenosine deaminase (ADA) is needed for the immune system to work (T-lymphocytes).\nIts lack causes dysfunction of the immune system (SCID); gene therapy was first tried for it.\nAddison's disease is adrenal cortex hyposecretion and Parkinson's disease affects the nervous system."}
